    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3462" root="بهو" body-key="b">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَا</span></b> , (JK, Msb, K,) aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَبْهَا</span>, (JK,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَبْهُو</span>;
(Msb, K;) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهُوَ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَبْهُو</span>; and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهِىَ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَبْهَى</span>;
(S, * K;) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَى</span>, [first pers. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَيْتُ</span>,] aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَبْهَى</span>;
(K;) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَآءٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَآءَةٌ</span>; (JK, TA;) <i>He</i> (a
man, S) or <i>it, was, </i> or <i>became, characterized by,</i>
or <i>possessed of,</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَآء</span>, meaning <i>beauty,</i> or <i>goodliness</i>
[&amp;c.]. (JK, S, Msb, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَوْتُهُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَيْتُهُ</span>: see
3. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهِىَ</span>, (S, K,) aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَوَ</span></b> , (K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهًا</span>, (TA,)
<i>It</i> (a tent, S, K) <i>was,</i> or <i>became, empty,</i> or
<i>vacant:</i> (K:) or <i>it was,</i> or <i>became, rent,</i> or
<i>pierced with holes, and rendered vacant.</i> (S,
TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهِىَ بِهِ</span> <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَأَ بِهِ</span> [q. v.]. (JK.) And
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَؤُوا بِهِ</span> occurs in a trad., as they relate it, for
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَهَؤُوا بِهِ</span>. (A'Obeyd, TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بهأ</span>.)

